      <memberdef kind="variable" id="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_v_g_split_group_config_1afa1fede04d255fc720b9bc56c67b1a80" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::vector&lt; std::string &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::vector&lt;std::string&gt; AGRemapCore::VGSplitGroupConfig::ibPaths</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>ibPaths</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::VGSplitGroupConfig::ibPaths</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The source ``.ib`` of every drawn object, in draw order. The split needs all of them even
when this group holds only one: a cut component&apos;s vertex set is the union over every
object&apos;s kept triangles, so a group that saw one object would write a blend the other
object&apos;s index buffer cannot index. Empty: the group&apos;s own ``ib`` members, in member order
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/AGRemapCore/model/iniresources/VGSplitGroupResource.h" line="112" column="21" bodyfile="include/AGRemapCore/model/iniresources/VGSplitGroupResource.h" bodystart="112" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="struct_a_g_remap_core_1_1_v_g_split_group_config_1ad75ebe60410e2eec68015719fe4a3a0b" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::unordered_map&lt; std::string, std::size_t &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::unordered_map&lt;std::string, std::size_t&gt; AGRemapCore::VGSplitGroupConfig::ibBytesPerIndex</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>ibBytesPerIndex</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::VGSplitGroupConfig::ibBytesPerIndex</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
How many bytes one index takes, keyed by the source ``.ib`` path -- 2 for a buffer its
``.ini`` declares ``DXGI_FORMAT_R16_UINT``. A path that is not here is 4, which is every
mod that does not say otherwise.

The width is carried rather than inferred because it CANNOT be inferred: a 16-bit buffer
whose byte count divides by 12 reads as 32-bit without complaint, at half the index count
and with values past the end of the mesh. See :cpp:class:`AGRemapCore::IbFile`
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
